    <!-- Engineering Philosophy Section -->
    <section id="philosophy" class="philosophy">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <span class="section-tag">Engineering Philosophy</span>
                <h2 class="section-title">How I Build Software</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Principles that guide my engineering decisions</p>
            </div>

            <div class="philosophy-grid">
                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-expand-arrows-alt"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Scalability First</h3>
                    <p>Building systems that handle growth gracefully. Whether it's 100 or 100,000 requests per second, the architecture should scale horizontally and vertically without complete rewrites.</p>
                    <div class="philosophy-example">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> Designed billing infrastructure to process thousands of transactions daily with room for 10x growth.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-tools"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Maintainability</h3>
                    <p>Code is read more than it's written. I prioritize clean code, modular design, and comprehensive documentation to make systems easy to understand and modify.</p>
                    <div class="philosophy-example">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> Architected modular codebase using ActiveRecord patterns, reducing technical debt and bug rates.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-eye"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Observability</h3>
                    <p>You can't improve what you can't measure. I implement logging, metrics, and monitoring from day one to debug issues quickly and make data-driven decisions.</p>
                    <div class="philosophy-example">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> Identified and eliminated slow queries through systematic performance monitoring.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-project-diagram"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3>API Design Excellence</h3>
                    <p>Great APIs are intuitive, consistent, and well-documented. I design endpoints that follow RESTful principles and provide excellent developer experience.</p>
                    <div class="philosophy-example">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> Reduced API onboarding time by 60% through comprehensive Swagger documentation.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-tachometer-alt"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Performance Engineering</h3>
                    <p>Performance is a feature, not an afterthought. I optimize at every layer — from database queries to API responses — to deliver sub-100ms response times.</p>
                    <div class="philosophy-example">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> Slashed API response time by 50% through intelligent caching and query optimization.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="philosophy-card">
                    <div class="philosophy-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-vial"></i>
                    </div>
                    <h3>Test-Driven Development</h3>
                    <p>Tests are my safety net. I write comprehensive unit and integration tests using RSpec to catch bugs early and refactor with confidence.</p>
                    <div class="philosophy-example">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> Maintained high test coverage ensuring 99.9% uptime in production systems.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- What I Care About -->
            <div class="care-about">
                <h3>Things I Care About in Backend Development</h3>
                <div class="care-grid">
                    <div class="care-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i>
                        <span>Database Query Optimization</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="care-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i>
